# Gate 4 whitelist — names with no production reference.
#
# Two rules, both enforced:
#   1. Every entry needs a reason after the '#'.
#   2. An entry deferring to future wiring must name the TASK that wires it,
#      and the gate FAILS once that task completes. Debt cannot outlive its
#      task; the list shrinks by construction.
#
# History: 43 -> 20 (an over-broad first pass, corrected) -> 13 (T056 closed)
# -> 3 (feature complete). The last drop exposed four release entry conditions
# that were implemented and never called by the loop — quiet hours would have
# deferred firings that nothing released.
#
# What remains are read surfaces for operators. Not deferred, so no task:
# they are not waiting on anything.

describe          # runtime inspection of presence (FR-023); read by operators
entries           # audit log read side; read by operators and by tests
count             # fingerprint store size; read by operators and by tests

# Election entry points. Called from app/gateway/trigger_engine_wiring.py, the
# composition root — which lives OUTSIDE this module because Gate 1 bans the
# engine from importing agent core, and assembling the engine needs AppConfig.
# Gate 4's scope is this module, so a caller on the gateway side is invisible to
# it. Not deferred; nothing is waiting on these.
build_lock        # chooses the lock backend from database config; called by the composition root
acquire           # SingleRunnerLock.acquire; called by the composition root during election
